Func:LCAO/nbspline=10; Sys:AsGa; Ref:energy,force,stress

The stress fingerprint uses the same order-10 interpolated structure factors
as the Ewald energy. The previous fingerprint, 60277.381032 kbar, combined
interpolated energy/force terms with Ewald stress from direct atomic phases.
Reusing the interpolated SF changes the absolute-component stress sum to
60277.308036 kbar. Energy, force, input and comparison tolerances are unchanged.

The coarse 15x15x15 grid and As/Ga valence charges 15/13 give a maximum Ewald
component difference of 0.02409268 kbar relative to direct SF. This case is
an order-10 interpolation regression, not a direct-SF accuracy benchmark.
MODULE_PW_stress_ewa includes a six-direction energy/strain derivative test
for this exact cell, grid and order. At neighboring strain steps 3e-5/1e-5,
the measured maximum errors are 3.74e-5/1.50e-5 kbar. These checks validate
the reference change against the corresponding discrete Ewald energy.
